to, again just like empathy

00:39:11.510 --> 00:39:14.770
or like feeling someone's
pain is just something

00:39:14.770 --> 00:39:17.720
that just comes out of 'em.

00:39:17.720 --> 00:39:19.100
This is my wife.

00:39:19.100 --> 00:39:21.420
But so for you it's interesting that

00:39:21.420 --> 00:39:25.494
in making that effort, I would
imagine there was a roadblock

00:39:25.494 --> 00:39:28.030
and I guess I've experienced
this too that like

00:39:28.030 --> 00:39:32.220
there's an added roadblock
of a self-awareness

00:39:32.220 --> 00:39:35.307
that's like there's a
vulnerability to even trying

00:39:35.307 --> 00:39:37.300
that makes it even more difficult, right.

00:39:37.300 --> 00:39:40.530
It's like now all of a sudden I'm gonna,

00:39:40.530 --> 00:39:42.990
instead of hanging up and
saying, "Love you, Mom,"

00:39:42.990 --> 00:39:44.113
I'm gonna say,

00:39:46.137 --> 00:39:48.710
"How do you feel?" or I'm
gonna make the decision

00:39:48.710 --> 00:39:52.840
to share how what she
shared with me made me feel.

00:39:52.840 --> 00:39:54.730
I'm gonna share that with her.

00:39:54.730 --> 00:39:58.195
And then it's like, I'm gonna do this now

00:39:58.195 --> 00:40:00.378
and it's gonna feel weird to me.

00:40:00.378 --> 00:40:03.190
It might feel weird to my mom.

00:40:03.190 --> 00:40:07.890
It might, like what's my
