00:47:14.480 --> 00:47:17.140
in the same way that someone might wear,

00:47:17.140 --> 00:47:19.175
oh I've got this little rubber band

00:47:19.175 --> 00:47:22.700
that every time I see it,
I think be in the heart,

00:47:22.700 --> 00:47:27.353
you know, there's some kind
of physical clue or a--

00:47:30.210 --> 00:47:32.000
Maybe a tattoo of a heart.

00:47:32.000 --> 00:47:33.930
Something that helps you.
On your heart.

00:47:33.930 --> 00:47:35.360
No there's a word for that

00:47:35.360 --> 00:47:37.160
but I don't know exactly what it is.

00:47:38.340 --> 00:47:43.340
I think that if I look at
a picture of the future me

00:47:45.180 --> 00:47:47.280
and it's the more embodied me,

00:47:47.280 --> 00:47:51.123
he has long hair and a
beard, and a long beard.

00:47:55.080 --> 00:47:57.560
Why?

00:47:57.560 --> 00:47:59.880
Well, you know, you think about someone

00:47:59.880 --> 00:48:04.570
who has thrown caution to the wind

00:48:04.570 --> 00:48:07.000
and is sort of just
trying to be in concert

00:48:07.000 --> 00:48:11.107
with the forces of the
universe and is a member,

00:48:12.220 --> 00:48:15.763
is an interdependent member
of the global community,

00:48:16.640 --> 00:48:20.947
there's a reason that you
see somebody with long hair

00:48:20.947 --> 00:48:23.720
and a beard and you're like,
they're either homeless

00:48:25.240 --> 00:48:28.780
or Jesus.

00:48:28.780 --> 00:48:30.627
You know what I'm saying.
Or--

00:48:31.470 --> 00:48:32.520
Or--

00:48:32.520 --> 00:48:34.170
You're saying enlightened?

00:48:34.170 --> 00:48:35.773
No, no, no no no no no.

00:48:35.773 --> 00:48:37.770
I'm not saying enlightened by any means,

00:48:37.770 --> 00:48:42.540
I'm just saying that they kinda
look like they're not trying

00:48:42.540 --> 00:48:47.540
a whole lot to get
everything exactly trimmed up

00:48:48.270 --> 00:48:50.400
and combed in exactly the right way

00:48:50.400 --> 00:48:53.800
to then get into the
mold that people expect.

00:48:53.800 --> 00:48:56.200
But I also think that--
So you're saying grooming--

00:48:56.200 --> 00:48:57.790
There's a reason--
There's a correlation

00:48:57.790 --> 00:48:59.359
between grooming and--
I think this

00:48:59.359 --> 00:49:00.192
is pretty simple.
And yeah, I'm just,

00:49:00.192 --> 00:49:02.420
just to state it simply.
If you go to Woodstock,

00:49:02.420 --> 00:49:04.230
you didn't see a lot of
people with buzz cuts

00:49:04.230 --> 00:49:05.490
and military-style hair cuts.

00:49:05.490 --> 00:49:09.840
It was like long hair,
beard, hippie, no bras.

00:49:09.840 --> 00:49:13.550
It's a relaxing of
standards and a relaxing

00:49:13.550 --> 00:49:17.390
of trying to hold some sort of mold

00:49:17.390 --> 00:49:20.370
and fit into a certain thing.

00:49:20.370 --> 00:49:23.410
Now, again, we'll talk about
how, well they actually became,

00:49:23.410 --> 00:49:25.710
the counter-culture became
the culture in a lot of ways

00:49:25.710 --> 00:49:29.850
and sub-cultures become
oppressive cultures

00:49:29.850 --> 00:49:31.989
that expect people to
do something to fit in.

00:49:31.989 --> 00:49:32.880
We're not talking about that.
But to state it simply,

00:49:32.880 --> 00:49:37.880
a lack of, a loosening of
outward perceived grooming

00:49:41.964 --> 00:49:46.383
is a reflection of more
of an inward grooming.

00:49:47.440 --> 00:49:49.610
Like spending your energy

00:49:49.610 --> 00:49:52.790
on not how other people
perceive you externally

00:49:52.790 --> 00:49:55.670
but how you perceive yourself internally.

00:49:55.670 --> 00:49:56.650
Yeah.

00:49:56.650 --> 00:49:58.047
Okay.
Yeah, it's the,

00:50:00.079 --> 00:50:01.470
again, it's the--
Which is different

